---
// The intro page; the demo app is at /demo/ (built with DEMO_BASE=/velo/demo/ and copied into site/dist/demo by docs:build).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="Demo · velo" description="Try velo in your browser: the real interface over a made-up notes folder.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Demo</h1>
    <p class="lede">The real velo interface, running in your browser over a made-up notes folder.</p>
    <p><a class="button" href={`${base}/demo/`}>Open the demo</a></p>

    <h2>What is different</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Nothing is saved: everything stays in the page, and a reload starts over.</li>
      <li>Search is simplified: it matches words and titles, but it is not the app’s full-text index.</li>
      <li>One note is locked. Its passphrase is <code>demo</code>.</li>
      <li>Things that need your computer (choosing a folder, Finder, the global shortcuts, agents) are stand-ins or absent.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Things to try</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><kbd>⌘P</kbd> (Ctrl+P): the command palette, every action by name.</li>
      <li><kbd>⌘L</kbd> (Ctrl+L): back to the search box; type to filter, Enter to open.</li>
      <li><kbd>⌘⇧T</kbd> (Ctrl+Shift+T): the Filters panel, to combine tags and saved searches.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>More in the <a href={`${base}/shortcuts/`}>shortcuts</a> and the <a href={`${base}/recipes/`}>recipes</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
